`GET /v1/auth/oauth/scopes`

Lists the business permissions available to OAuth applications.

<Tabs>
<Tab title="TypeScript">
```typescript TypeScript
photon.auth.listOauthScopes(input?: ListOauthScopesInput, options?: RequestOptions): Promise<ListOauthScopesOutput>
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Python">
```python Python
photon.auth.list_oauth_scopes(input: ListOauthScopesInput | None = None) -> models.ListOauthScopesResponse
```
</Tab>
<Tab title="Rust">
```rust Rust
client.list_oauth_scopes().await -> Result<ResponseValue<types::ListOauthScopesResponse>, Error<ListOauthScopesError>>
```
</Tab>
</Tabs>

<RequestExample>
```typescript TypeScript
import { Photon } from "@photon-ai/api";

const photon = new Photon();
const result = await photon.auth.listOauthScopes();
```

```python Python
from photon_api import Photon

photon = Photon()
result = photon.auth.list_oauth_scopes()
```

```rust Rust
use photon_ai_api::PhotonClientBuilder;

let client = PhotonClientBuilder::new().build()?;
let result = client
    .list_oauth_scopes()
    .await
    .map_err(|error| format!("{error:?}"))?
    .into_inner();
```

</RequestExample>

<ResponseExample>
```json 200
{
  "scopes": [
    "string"
  ]
}
```

</ResponseExample>

## Returns

**`200`** The configurable OAuth business permissions. ListOauthScopesResponse

<ResponseField name="scopes" type={"array of string"} required>
Business permissions an OAuth application can be configured with. Client creation and scope updates accept only these values. OIDC protocol scopes (openid, profile, email, offline_access) are not included.
</ResponseField>

